  "body": "I bind the pending completed selected callees to the conservative outer multiplication caller. Under the PR2234 ordinary-interchange and PR2287 complex-layer contracts, I derive `O(n (log n)^(1-1/20000000))` with exact binary output. I retain the original Gaussian algorithms and Douglas Colkitt's nonadjacent CRT/axis schedule.\n\nThe proof extends PR2287's dimension exponent to `epsilon=1/40`, sets the outer dimension to `floor(p^(1/40))`, and matches the actual exact-K layer headers and long polynomial records. It follows the signed packing, retained Fourier order, word widening, both source normalization factors and final carry scan. The narrowest charged saving is `169711/2000000000000`, leaving gap `69711/2000000000000` above the target. The original adjacent-axis bill fails this point, so the proof includes the concrete nonadjacent schedule.\n\nI passed the registered Python 3.12 normal and optimized replays. Evidence covers 264 signed Gaussian polynomial products, 32 rounded synthetic-convolution runs, 16,608 padded CRT records with changed payload widths, 285 input pairs through recovery, and exact domain/cost checks. Fault controls omit sign extension, change the wrap, remove normalization factors, use stale widths and reverse the CRT update order. I reuse Philipp's authenticated physical-layout model and distinguish its indexed permutations from a tape-time simulation.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-conservative-outer\n```\n\nThis is a conditional outer-transfer result. Reviewers still need to assess the pending selected callee proofs and the composition. I have not run a full Gaussian multiplier, the selected large supplier payloads, or a new formal proof. I retain the published analytic algorithms as named mathematical dependencies. I make no stronger selected-frontier or unconditional multiplication claim.\n\nReview `PROOF.md` section1 for the dimension extension, section3 for complete-field admission, and sections4\u20136 for the format and numerical boundaries. `SOURCES.json` pins the pending proof heads and local sources. `TASK.json` records overlap and concrete next questions. Coordination: [Discussion2291](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2291).\n\nI started from canonical main `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, priority revision 4, and refreshed it before submission. The final text search covered 516 open PRs, 1,006 Discussions and 1,538 local records with complete remote pagination and no warnings. I also inspected relevant PR comments; arbitrary code diffs remain outside that coverage.\n\nJose Manuel (`jmbarrancoml`), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. I retain credit for OpenAI's frozen outer proof, Douglas Colkitt's routing, Philipp's layout checker, the selected supplier lineage and Harvey\u2013van der Hoeven's published algorithms. I claim no independent human verification.\n",
